 Snippet: The British Cheese Board once claimed that Britain had about 700 distinct local cheeses.^[48]^ France and Italy have perhaps 400 each; a French proverb says there is a different French cheese for every day of the year; and Charles de Gaulle once asked "how can you govern a country in which there are 246 kinds of cheese?".^[49]^

